{"sequence":28,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T08:10:02.199905759Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b9bf2e92","body":"Apply the same division-by-zero guard to ca_min_mg_per_l and mg_min_mg_per_l that was applied to gh_min_d. In update_molt_stress (shrimp.rs:459,464), ca_stress and mg_stress divide by params.ca_min_mg_per_l and params.mg_min_mg_per_l respectively without a .max(0.01) guard. Similarly, molt_mineral_modifier (shrimp.rs:1559-1560) divides by ca_min_mg_per_l and mg_min_mg_per_l without guards. If a user sets these parameters to zero (as the test_zero_gh_min_parameter_uses_defensive_guard test exercises for gh_min_d), NaN/Inf propagates through stress and molt calculations.","dedup_key":"1ea6dd49bcc653d432af9c0b6f739c37db32d8f6dd38575da06168b301d2daf7","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":29,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T08:10:02.204660763Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-4af528d5","body":"The new snapshot-side `dominant_repro_suppression` implementation in `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:375` does not match the real reproduction model. It omits the molt-stress factor used by `update_reproductive_readiness` at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:679`, folds TAN and nitrite into a generic `chemistry` bucket instead of the separate `tan`/`nitrite` diagnostics in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:1572` and `:1574`, and uses different suppression curves/floors than the shared helper starting at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:1548`. Even after the compile error is fixed, `repro_dominant_suppression` can disagree with the actual readiness calculation and mislead debugging.","dedup_key":"01a9cfe01e6882d062208f72b656d2d5b81127ca9638c3a828c88f62ea18169c","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
