{"sequence":70,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T09:57:46.891514819Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-9708b232","body":"In `e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs`, the `all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` test (#[test]) calls the same `run_probe_*` functions that the 5 individual `#[test]` probe functions also call. When `cargo test` runs the full file, each expensive probe (multi-day simulations) executes twice: once in its own test and once in the summary. Either gate the individual tests behind a feature flag / `#[ignore]` when the summary runner exists, or have the summary runner reuse test results rather than re-executing. This doubles CI wall-clock time for no additional coverage.","dedup_key":"8bd27f212b31132dd7b57ef14c1dc09774860b55cfbd692b90f6f9a8af133152","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":71,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T09:57:46.901291577Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-f084dd66","body":"P1: `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate.rs:99-113` computes `root_oxygenation_bonus_cm` against the full substrate depth and only clamps after adding it to `base_penetration_cm`. When the base penetration already spans the whole bed (for example the low-demand path at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate.rs:182-183`), the breakdown can report a positive root bonus even though `effective_penetration_cm` is unchanged. That makes the exposed tracing/debug metric incorrect and turns the intended smooth saturation into a hard clip near fully oxic beds. The reported bonus should be capped to the remaining available depth, or recomputed as `effective_penetration_cm - base_penetration_cm`.","dedup_key":"053d4d4b02f0e0a4197614edf67a993a58b152965d60ffbefaa4bc57213a40c2","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
