{"sequence":84,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T10:30:36.020139308Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-6-5c9d4bed","body":"In `root_oxygenation_active_biomass_g()` (substrate.rs:140), `compute_habitat_registry(state)` recomputes the full habitat registry from scratch on every call. Within the engine tick loop, `step_substrate_zones()` is called after `refresh_habitat_registry()` has already updated `state.habitat_registry`. Consider accepting the registry as a parameter or using `state.habitat_registry` directly within the hot path, and only falling back to recomputation in the standalone `root_oxygenation_bonus_cm()` public accessor which may be called with stale state from tracing/test code.","dedup_key":"595e8a2f39614e4fa4f252ccb8a5cd00a67fbc39678143ea5cec689e036fc104","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":85,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T10:30:36.029518850Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-6-8b38a232","body":"The comment block for integration test `planted_substrate_denitrification_interaction` (root_zone_oxygenation.rs:131-133) states 'planted substrate shows more N₂ export from denitrification (deeper oxic zone → larger suboxic zone pushed deeper → more capacity)'. This reasoning is incorrect: deeper oxic zone means *less* suboxic volume, leading to *less* denitrification per hour, as correctly demonstrated by `root_oxygenation_reduces_hourly_denitrification_when_it_shrinks_suboxic_volume` (line 168). The test assertion itself only checks for divergence (abs difference > 0.001) which is correct, but the comment misattributes the direction of the effect and could mislead future developers.","dedup_key":"f934b385052f2ffe313a5dd8ddfcf4f1cd94d40cb38680731cf64cfef952d2a8","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":86,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T10:30:36.038799124Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-6-e14eeefd","body":"Restore the rooted-plant O₂ demand term in the E4a base calculation, or otherwise preserve the old E4a baseline before adding the new ROL modifier. In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate.rs:208-238`, `estimate_substrate_o2_demand_rate()` now excludes rooted biomass entirely, so the new `effective_penetration = base + bonus` path is not actually an additive hook on top of the existing model anymore. A planted bed with `rol_rate_cm_per_g = 0` now collapses to the same substrate-oxygen baseline as an unplanted bed, instead of retaining the preexisting root-respiration O₂ demand. That changes the meaning of the base model and makes the new parameter absorb two effects at once: added root O₂ supply and removed root O₂ consumption.","dedup_key":"ff8f32f62ff27a3515d18ae462c7f9d2fc4d9e8b3c4b7cc82e2c9b6ffbb2f2d5","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
